Add ``safe_mro`` and use it wherever a checker only walks a class's MRO to look
something up. Duplicate or inconsistent bases leave a class without an MRO, and
the error raised in their place used to abort the whole file with a fatal
``astroid-error`` instead of reporting the offences the file does have. This
affects ``invalid-name``, ``stop-iteration-return`` and the ``__slots__`` checks.

Refs #11272
